STUDENT TASK MANAGEMENT SYSTEM — REQUIREMENTS

1. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

FR-01 Authentication: Students can register, sign in, sign out, and recover access using the configured authentication method.
FR-02 Create task: An authenticated student can create a task with a required title and optional description, due date, course/category, and priority.
FR-03 View tasks: Students can view their task list and task details. The list supports filtering and sorting by status, due date, course/category, and priority.
FR-04 Update task: A student can edit the fields of a task they own and save the changes.
FR-05 Track completion: A student can mark a task complete and reopen it if that behavior is enabled.
FR-06 Delete task: A student can delete a task they own after confirming the action.
FR-07 Validate input: The system validates required and malformed values and gives actionable feedback.
FR-08 Enforce ownership: Students cannot view or change another student's tasks. Administrative access, if any, must be explicitly authorized.
FR-09 Persist data: Saved tasks and updates remain available across sessions until deleted under the system's retention policy.
FR-10 Report operation status: The system reports success only after an operation is saved and clearly reports failures.

2. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

NFR-01 Usability: Core task actions are understandable and usable on supported mobile and desktop screen sizes.
NFR-02 Performance: Under an agreed workload, 95% of task-list and task-operation requests should complete within 2 seconds; workload and test environment must be specified.
NFR-03 Security: Use secure authentication, protect data in transit and at rest, validate inputs server-side, and enforce authorization for every task operation.
NFR-04 Privacy: Collect only necessary data and follow a documented retention and deletion policy.
NFR-05 Accessibility: Support keyboard navigation, visible focus, labeled controls, and accessible status/error messages; target WCAG 2.2 AA.
NFR-06 Reliability: Failed requests must not appear successful; preserve entered data where practicable and allow safe retries.
NFR-07 Compatibility: Document and test supported browsers, operating systems, and device requirements.
NFR-08 Availability: Define an availability target, maintenance windows, backup approach, and recovery objectives with stakeholders.
NFR-09 Maintainability: Record operational errors without logging passwords or unnecessary sensitive task content.

3. USER STORIES

US-01 As a student, I want to create a task so that I can record academic work.
US-02 As a student, I want to sort and filter my tasks so that I can find and prioritize work.
US-03 As a student, I want to edit a task when assignment details change so that my plan stays accurate.
US-04 As a student, I want to mark a task complete so that I can distinguish finished work from pending work.
US-05 As a student, I want to delete an obsolete task with confirmation so that I can keep my list relevant without accidental loss.
US-06 As a student, I want my saved tasks available after signing in again so that I can continue across sessions.

4. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA — MAIN CRUD OPERATIONS

CREATE
- Given an authenticated student, when they submit a non-empty title and valid optional values, then exactly one task is saved and appears in their list.
- Given a missing title or invalid value, when they submit, then the field is identified, no task is created, and other entered values are retained where practicable.
- If saving fails, the system reports failure and does not show a success state.

READ
- Given an authenticated student, when they open their task list, then only tasks they are authorized to access are displayed.
- When they open a task, then its saved fields and current status are displayed.
- If there are no tasks or no filter matches, the system shows a clear empty state.
- For an unknown task ID or another student's task, the system does not disclose task contents and returns an appropriate not-found or access-denied response.

UPDATE
- Given the task owner and valid changes, when they save, then the changes persist and appear in both list and detail views.
- Given invalid changes, then errors are identified and the previously saved task remains unchanged.
- If another session has changed the task, the system prevents silent overwriting and prompts the student to refresh or resolve the conflict.
- An unauthorized update or update to an unknown task ID changes no data.

DELETE
- When the owner chooses delete, the system requests confirmation before removal.
- If the student cancels, the task remains unchanged.
- If the student confirms, the task is removed from the active list and success is reported; subsequent retrieval follows the documented deletion policy.
- If deletion fails or the requester is unauthorized, the system reports no false success and does not disclose protected data.

5. EDGE CASES

- Empty or whitespace-only title; very long text; unsupported characters.
- Missing, malformed, past, or boundary-time due dates; timezone and daylight-saving changes.
- Double submission or retry after a timeout causing a potential duplicate task.
- Network loss or server error during any operation.
- Simultaneous edits from multiple devices, or deletion while the task is open elsewhere.
- Empty lists, filters with no results, and equal or missing due dates during sorting.
- Session expiry during submission, or navigation away with unsaved changes.
- Repeated completion toggles or reopening an already completed task.
- Attempts to access another student's task by guessing or reusing an identifier.
- Very large task lists and pagination/loading behavior.
- Account deletion or retention expiry while tasks still exist.

6. UNANSWERED QUESTIONS

- Is the product for individual students only, or are instructor/admin roles and shared or assigned tasks required?
- Which authentication and account recovery methods are required?
- Are course/category, priority, reminders, attachments, recurring tasks, subtasks, or notes in scope?
- What task statuses are supported, and can completed tasks be reopened or archived?
- Are due dates date-only or time-specific, and which timezone is authoritative?
- Is deletion permanent, recoverable, or subject to a retention period?
- Are notifications required; if so, which channels, schedules, and controls?
- Which platforms and browsers are supported, and what user volume, availability, and performance targets apply?
- What privacy, accessibility, audit, or regulatory obligations apply?
- Are export, search, calendar synchronization, or learning-management-system integrations required?
- What happens to unsaved edits after session expiry or when leaving a form?
const express = require("express");
const helmet = require("helmet");
const bcrypt = require("bcryptjs");
const jwt = require("jsonwebtoken");
const Database = require("better-sqlite3");
const { z } = require("zod");
const { randomUUID } = require("node:crypto");

if (!process.env.JWT_SECRET || process.env.JWT_SECRET.length < 32) {
  throw new Error("Set JWT_SECRET to a random string of at least 32 characters.");
}

const app = express();
const db = new Database("student-tasks.db");

app.use(helmet());
app.use(express.json({ limit: "20kb" }));

db.pragma("journal_mode = WAL");
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password_hash TEXT NOT NULL
  );

  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    owner_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    course TEXT,
    priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'medium',
    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',
    due_date TEXT,
    version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL
  );

  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS idempotency_keys (
    owner_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    key TEXT NOT NULL,
    task_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (owner_id, key)
  );

  CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS tasks_owner_idx ON tasks(owner_id);
`);

const taskFields = {
  title: z.string().trim().min(1).max(200),
  description: z.string().max(5000).nullable().optional(),
  course: z.string().trim().max(120).nullable().optional(),
  priority: z.enum(["low", "medium", "high"]).optional(),
  status: z.enum(["pending", "completed"]).optional(),
  dueDate: z.string().regex(/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/).nullable().optional(),
};

function validDate(value) {
  if (value == null) return true;
  const date = new Date(`${value}T00:00:00.000Z`);
  return !Number.isNaN(date.getTime()) &&
    date.toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value;
}

const createSchema = z.object(taskFields).refine(
  (value) => validDate(value.dueDate),
  { message: "Use a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format.", path: ["dueDate"] }
);

const updateSchema = z.object({
  ...taskFields,
  version: z.number().int().positive(),
}).partial().refine(
  (value) => Object.keys(value).some((key) => key !== "version"),
  { message: "Provide at least one task field to update." }
).refine(
  (value) => validDate(value.dueDate),
  { message: "Use a valid date in YYYY-MM-DD format.", path: ["dueDate"] }
);

function publicTask(row) {
  return {
    id: row.id,
    title: row.title,
    description: row.description,
    course: row.course,
    priority: row.priority,
    status: row.status,
    dueDate: row.due_date,
    version: row.version,
    createdAt: row.created_at,
    updatedAt: row.updated_at,
  };
}

function authenticate(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.replace(/^Bearer\s+/i, "");
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: "Sign in required." });

  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    next();
  } catch {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: "Invalid or expired session." });
  }
}

app.post("/api/auth/register", async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const input = z.object({
      email: z.string().trim().email().max(254),
      password: z.string().min(12).max(128),
    }).parse(req.body);

    const id = randomUUID();
    const email = input.email.toLowerCase();
    const passwordHash = await bcrypt.hash(input.password, 12);
    db.prepare("INSERT INTO users (id, email, password_hash) VALUES (?, ?, ?)")
      .run(id, email, passwordHash);

    res.status(201).json({ id, email });
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.code === "SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE") {
      return res.status(409).json({ error: "That email is already registered." });
    }
    next(error);
  }
});

app.post("/api/auth/login", async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const input = z.object({
      email: z.string().trim().email(),
      password: z.string().min(1).max(128),
    }).parse(req.body);

    const user = db.prepare("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?")
      .get(input.email.toLowerCase());

    if (!user || !(await bcrypt.compare(input.password, user.password_hash))) {
      return res.status(401).json({ error: "Email or password is incorrect." });
    }

    const token = jwt.sign(
      { sub: user.id },
      process.env.JWT_SECRET,
      { expiresIn: "1h" }
    );
    res.json({ token });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});

app.get("/api/tasks", authenticate, (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const querySchema = z.object({
      status: z.enum(["pending", "completed"]).optional(),
      priority: z.enum(["low", "medium", "high"]).optional(),
      course: z.string().max(120).optional(),
      sort: z.enum(["dueDate", "priority", "status", "course", "createdAt"]).default("dueDate"),
      order: z.enum(["asc", "desc"]).default("asc"),
      page: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).default(1),
      limit: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).max(100).default(20),
    }).parse(req.query);

    const columns = {
      dueDate: "due_date",
      priority: "priority",
      status: "status",
      course: "course",
      createdAt: "created_at",
    };

    const conditions = ["owner_id = ?"];
    const values = [req.user.sub];

    for (const field of ["status", "priority", "course"]) {
      if (querySchema[field] !== undefined) {
        conditions.push(`${field} = ?`);
        values.push(querySchema[field]);
      }
    }

    const where = conditions.join(" AND ");
    const total = db.prepare(`SELECT COUNT(*) AS count FROM tasks WHERE ${where}`)
      .get(...values).count;
    const offset = (querySchema.page - 1) * querySchema.limit;

    const rows = db.prepare(`
      SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE ${where}
      ORDER BY ${columns[querySchema.sort]} ${querySchema.order.toUpperCase()}, id ASC
      LIMIT ? OFFSET ?
    `).all(...values, querySchema.limit, offset);

    res.json({
      items: rows.map(publicTask),
      total,
      page: querySchema.page,
      limit: querySchema.limit,
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});

app.post("/api/tasks", authenticate, (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const input = createSchema.parse(req.body);
    const key = req.get("Idempotency-Key");

    if (key && (key.length < 8 || key.length > 128)) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: "Idempotency-Key must be 8–128 characters." });
    }

    if (key) {
      const prior = db.prepare(`
        SELECT task_id FROM idempotency_keys WHERE owner_id = ? AND key = ?
      `).get(req.user.sub, key);

      if (prior) {
        const existing = db.prepare(
          "SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = ?"
        ).get(prior.task_id, req.user.sub);
        if (!existing) return res.status(409).json({ error: "This retry key was already used." });
        return res.status(200).json(publicTask(existing));
      }
    }

    const now = new Date().toISOString();
    const id = randomUUID();

    const save = db.transaction(() => {
      db.prepare(`
        INSERT INTO tasks
          (id, owner_id, title, description, course, priority, status, due_date, created_at, updated_at)
        VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)
      `).run(
        id, req.user.sub, input.title, input.description ?? null,
        input.course ?? null, input.priority ?? "medium",
        input.status ?? "pending", input.dueDate ?? null, now, now
      );

      if (key) {
        db.prepare("INSERT INTO idempotency_keys (owner_id, key, task_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?)")
          .run(req.user.sub, key, id);
      }
    });

    save();
    const task = db.prepare("SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE id = ?").get(id);
    res.status(201).json(publicTask(task));
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});

app.get("/api/tasks/:id", authenticate, (req, res) => {
  const task = db.prepare("SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = ?")
    .get(req.params.id, req.user.sub);
  if (!task) return res.status(404).json({ error: "Task not found." });
  res.json(publicTask(task));
});

app.patch("/api/tasks/:id", authenticate, (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const input = updateSchema.parse(req.body);
    const task = db.prepare("SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = ?")
      .get(req.params.id, req.user.sub);

    if (!task) return res.status(404).json({ error: "Task not found." });
    if (input.version !== task.version) {
      return res.status(409).json({ error: "Task changed. Refresh before saving." });
    }

    const fields = {
      title: "title",
      description: "description",
      course: "course",
      priority: "priority",
      status: "status",
      dueDate: "due_date",
    };
    const updates = Object.keys(fields).filter((field) => input[field] !== undefined);

    const assignments = updates.map((field) => `${fields[field]} = ?`);
    const values = updates.map((field) =>
      field === "dueDate" ? input[field] : input[field]
    );

    assignments.push("version = version + 1", "updated_at = ?");
    values.push(new Date().toISOString(), req.params.id, req.user.sub, input.version);

    const result = db.prepare(`
      UPDATE tasks SET ${assignments.join(", ")}
      WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = ? AND version = ?
    `).run(...values);

    if (!result.changes) return res.status(409).json({ error: "Task changed. Refresh before saving." });

    res.json(publicTask(
      db.prepare("SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE id = ?").get(req.params.id)
    ));
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});

app.delete("/api/tasks/:id", authenticate, (req, res) => {
  const result = db.prepare("DELETE FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND owner_id = ?")
    .run(req.params.id, req.user.sub);
  if (!result.changes) return res.status(404).json({ error: "Task not found." });
  res.status(204).end();
});

app.use((error, req, res, next) => {
  if (error instanceof z.ZodError) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: "Please correct the highlighted fields.",
      fields: error.issues.map(({ path, message }) => ({
        field: path.join("."),
        message,
      })),
    });
  }
  console.error("Request failed:", error.message);
  res.status(500).json({ error: "The request could not be completed." });
});

const port = Number(process.env.PORT || 3000);
app.listen(port, () => console.log(`Task API listening on http://localhost:${port}`));